#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:1
msgid "The development loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Four commands, in this order, over and over. "
"{doc}`../../reference/cli/index` is the option-by-option reference; this "
"page is what the loop is *for*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:12
msgid "0. Before the loop: ask the documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:14
msgid ""
"The loop starts from a format that exists. Before that, the questions are"
" about the reports: is this an annual or a semi-annual report, where are "
"the totals, does the anchor you have in mind hold on the other reports of"
" the same issuer? `freeports-dev probe` answers the common ones on "
"several documents at once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:25
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A probe gives leads, not results — it takes the first match, which in a "
"financial report is often the table of contents. What it is good at is "
"showing, side by side, whether a label, a font or a position is **the "
"same in every report of the format**: an anchor that holds on one report "
"only is not an anchor. See {ref}`probe-subcommand` for the probes that "
"ship and for writing your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:30
msgid "1. `inspect-document` — which page is what"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:39
msgid ""
"**Run this first, and do not go past it until it is right.** If "
"classification is wrong, nothing downstream can be: a page that should be"
" `investments` and comes back as nothing is a classification bug, not an "
"extraction bug, and chasing it in `pdf_extract` is the single most common"
" way to lose an afternoon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:44
msgid "2. `inspect-page` — what the engine sees, stage by stage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:52
msgid ""
"The three pipeline modes in order, and the order is the method: each "
"shows what one segment made of the page, so the first one that looks "
"wrong is the segment to fix. This turns *\"the page is wrong\"* — a "
"question with no handle on it — into *\"`text_filter` dropped these "
"blocks\"*, which has one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "First wrong at"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "Look at"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "`pdf_blks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
#, python-brace-format
msgid "the layout selections: font, size, area ({doc}`selections`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "`txt_blks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "the filter: are the target companies matching? is the regex right?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "`results`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md
msgid "the deserializer: types, columns, units"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:62
msgid "Two more families of mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:64
msgid ""
"`table_md` / `table_ascii` render the PDF blocks **as a table**, with "
"their row and column metadata — which is how you check that the "
"tabularizer read the columns the way you read them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:66
msgid ""
"`structured` / `semistructured` / `unstructured` take `--strings` and "
"report which lines match, which is how you find out what font and size a "
"value is set in before writing a selection at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:69
msgid "What the last two modes are fed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:71
msgid ""
"`txt_blks` and `results` need a `filter_data` — what earlier iterations "
"of the job already extracted — and a `text_filter` that keeps only what "
"it can tie to a fund it has seen prints **nothing at all** when it is "
"given the wrong one. An empty printout is then indistinguishable from a "
"broken algorithm, which is the most expensive way this command can "
"mislead you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:76
msgid ""
"It therefore takes the first of three that exists, and says on its first "
"line which one it took:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:78
msgid ""
"`--filter-data`, which reads either a `.json` fixture — the same file the"
" suite reads — or a dill `.pkl`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:80
msgid ""
"the page type's own `tests/formats/<FORMAT>/[<n>/]pages/<page "
"type>/filter_data.json`, so that an inspection sees what the test sees;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:82
msgid ""
"the target list of the input database, which is what a first-iteration "
"page gets in a real run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:84
msgid ""
"If the file it names is not the one you meant — a format with several "
"documents has one fixture per variant — name it with `--filter-data` "
"instead of reading the empty output as a result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:87
msgid "3. `make-tests` — freeze a page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Writes the three per-page fixtures — PDF blocks, text blocks, results — "
"as **JSON** under `tests/formats/<FORMAT>/pages/`. JSON and readable on "
"purpose: a regression should be visible in a diff "
"({doc}`../../reference/design/blocks`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:98
msgid ""
"`make-tests` records **what the code does now**. It shows you what it is "
"about to write and asks; read it. Confirming a wrong result promotes a "
"bug into the specification, and from then on the test defends the bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:103
msgid ""
"Freeze a handful of representative pages, not every page: the first page "
"of a table, a continuation page, a page with an awkward row. Those are "
"where formats break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:106
msgid ""
"`make-tests` is also the honest way to **run** a pipeline on a page, "
"because it feeds the pipe exactly what the test will feed it. With "
"`--noconfirm` it keeps every file that already exists, fixture and "
"`filter_data.json` alike: to regenerate a page, delete its "
"`<page>-txt_blks.json` and `<page>-results.json` first. That is "
"deliberate in both directions — a hand-written `filter_data.json` can be "
"put in place *before* the fixture exists, and it will be found rather "
"than overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:113
msgid "4. `test` — run them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:122
msgid "Three kinds of test with very different costs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:124
msgid ""
"**Per-page tests** replay one page through one segment against its "
"fixture. Fast, run constantly, and they tell you *which segment of which "
"page* changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:127
msgid ""
"**The whole-document test** replays the entire report and compares the "
"output tables against `tests/formats/<FORMAT>/out/`. Slow, marked "
"`integration_tests`, and it is the one that actually says the format "
"works — the per-page fixtures can all pass while the schedule, the "
"promise resolution or the deduplication are wrong. It is `--slow`, or "
"`make test-slow`, and it is **not** in the default run: a command that "
"leaves it out says so in its last line, and `make ci-check` reports a "
"suite nobody ran at this commit as `NOT RUN` rather than as a pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:134
msgid ""
"**The classification test** runs `freeports classify` on each "
"`report.pdf` and passes when the report is recognised as the format of "
"its folder, or not recognised at all; recognised as another format fails."
" Slow, marked `classification_tests`, and part of `--slow` with the "
"whole-document test. It is what tells you that a rule in "
"`metadata/document_classify.yaml` has become too broad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/dev-loop.md:140
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`out/**` is the repository's **specification**, not a snapshot. If a run "
"diverges from it, the assumption is that the engine changed, not that the"
" expectation was wrong. Regenerating one of those files is a deliberate "
"act with a reason written down — never a way to make a red test green. It"
" is also what the grants of {doc}`../../overview/trust` are *about*: a "
"grant is a claim about the content of exactly those bytes."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Two kinds of test with very different costs:"
